{"packet_id":"D079-01","doc_id":"D079","jurisdiction":"San Francisco, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"San Francisco Rent Ordinance just cause eviction requirement","requirement":"A landlord must have a just cause reason, and that reason must be the dominant motive, to evict from a Rent Ordinance unit; mere lease expiration or a change in ownership is not just cause.","key_value":"17 just cause reasons","coverage_conditions":"Rental units covered by the Rent Ordinance. Tenancies exempt from the Ordinance's rent increase limits, such as units first obtaining a Certificate of Occupancy after June 13, 1979, Costa-Hawkins-eligible tenancies, and some rents regulated by another agency, remain subject to eviction provisions.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":"certificate_of_occupancy","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Covered Rent Ordinance units, plus tenancies exempt from rent increase limits (post-June 13, 1979 CofO units, Costa-Hawkins-eligible tenancies) for eviction purposes"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"A landlord who evicts or tries to evict a tenant unlawfully may be subject to substantial civil and/or criminal liability.","effective_date":null,"citation":"S.F. Admin. Code § 37.9","quoted_span":"In order to evict a tenant from a rental unit covered by the Rent Ordinance, a landlord must have a \"just cause\" reason that is the dominant motive for pursuing the eviction.","interaction":"Tenancies exempt from the Ordinance's rent increase limitations, including those eligible under the Costa-Hawkins Rental Housing Act, are still subject to its eviction provisions.","confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D079-01","doc_id":"D079","jurisdiction":"San Francisco, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Just cause required to remove housing services","requirement":"A landlord needs a just cause reason to take away or remove access to housing services such as garage, parking, driveway, storage and laundry facilities. Parking and storage may be temporarily removed for mandatory soft-story seismic retrofit work if Ordinance Section 37.2(r) is complied with.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental units covered by the Rent Ordinance; applies to access to housing services including garage facilities, parking facilities, driveways, storage spaces and laundry rooms.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Rent Ordinance covered units; housing services removal"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"S.F. Admin. Code § 37.9","quoted_span":"The landlord also needs a \"just cause“ reason to take away or remove access to certain housing services, including but not limited to garage facilities, parking facilities, driveways, storage spaces, and laundry rooms.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
